    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Winthrop was founded in 1857 when surveyor Alonzo P. Foster purchased 240 acres of prairie and platted 40 town lots, giving the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winthrop,_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Dubuque & Pacific Railroad reached Winthrop in 1859, and by 1868 it became the county’s second grain depot, boosting settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winthrop,_Iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Winthrop’s gently rolling hills, part of the Driftless Area, transition into fertile plains that have long supported Iowa’s agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Winthrop,_Iowa",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Situated between Independence and Manchester on Historic Route 20, Winthrop is known as one of northeast Iowa’s friendliest communities.",
